We examine the decay rates of $B_{c}^{+} ightarrow D^{*+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}^{+}$ and $B_{c}^{+} ightarrow D^{*+} 
u_{	au}^{+}$, as well as $B_{c}^{+} ightarrow D_{s}^{*+} 
u_{	au}^{+}$, in the context of the 3-flavor QCD model. We find that the decay widths of $B_{c}^{+} ightarrow D^{*+} 
u_{	au}^{+}$ and $B_{c}^{+} ightarrow D_{s}^{+} 
u_{	au}^{+}$ are significantly smaller than predicted by the heavy quark limit, and the branching fractions for these decays are on the order of $10^{-7}$.
